  "about": `# Iron Man Gauntlet - Mark 1

A wearable forearm gauntlet that flies a tiny drone by hand gesture: five flex sensors and two orientation sensors read the hand, and a radio module built into the arm sends the drone its sticks. It also opens armour plates on servos, fires a green and a red laser, lights a palm repulsor and finger LEDs, and carries a LiDAR, a thermal camera and a round touch screen.

This is the built arm: every part, pin, wire, resistor and capacitor of it, drawn from **designs/gauntlet.js**. Elbow on the left, fingertips on the right; the back of the hand above the palm.

**Try:** click the **ESP32** (the main board), then **Trace to battery** in the toolbar. Click any wire. Or pick two parts with **Map: Between selected**.`,
