    {"id":"paccs","name":"Accent splice","what":"The wire from GPIO 4 meets the three accent LEDs' resistors here.","desc":"W35 from GPIO 4 twisted and soldered with end 1 of R9, R10 and R11: four conductors, 14 mA.","zone":"palm","box":[3339,2118,40,40],"lab":"accent","lp":"r"},
    {"id":"pdivn","name":"Divider node","what":"Where the battery divider's two resistors meet: the wire to GPIO 35 reads the battery here.","desc":"Where R2 (100 k) and R3 (22 k, as built 2026-10-13) meet, with the white wire E20 to GPIO 35: the two resistors, the node and the wire under one adhesive heat-shrink sleeve. 8.7 V (a full LiHV pack) reads 1.57 V here, 6.6 V reads 1.19 V; the firmware's two-point calibration lives in config.h, the monitor-fault ceiling is 9.5 V.","warn":"A broken leg reads as a monitor FAULT, not as an empty pack: keep the leads short and the sleeve over both bodies.","zone":"elbow","area":"the elbow pocket","box":[561,1642,40,40],"lab":"divider node"}
